# Docs and rule consistency

This Cursor rule supplements the repository AGENTS.md instructions. It may add scoped requirements but may not weaken root security invariants.

**Authority:** [`docs/AGENTS.md`](../../docs/AGENTS.md) · root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md)

## When to update docs

Update docs **only** when behavior, architecture, security guarantees, public APIs, schemas, setup, or project status **actually changed**. Do not update docs merely because a code file was touched.

| Change type | Required doc update |
| ----------- | ------------------- |
| Vault schema change | [`VAULT_FORMAT.md`](../../docs/VAULT_FORMAT.md) |
| New security surface | [`SECURITY.md`](../../docs/SECURITY.md), [`THREAT_MODEL.md`](../../docs/THREAT_MODEL.md) |
| Architecture change | [`ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) |
| Feature status | [`ROADMAP.md`](../../docs/ROADMAP.md) — mark complete **only** with explicit permission |

Follow [`VAULT_FORMAT.md`](../../docs/VAULT_FORMAT.md) for envelope vs payload rules.

## Post-task documentation review

After completing an implementation task (before the final report), check whether these areas **need an update**. Update **only sections that changed** — never rewrite full documents for small diffs.

| Area | Check | Typical files |
| ---- | ----- | ------------- |
| README | User-facing features, quick start, or doc links changed? | `README.md`, `docs/README.md` |
| Architecture | Packages, data flow, crypto boundary, or UI layout changed? | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Security assumptions | New trust boundary, storage surface, or signing flow? | `docs/SECURITY.md`, `docs/THREAT_MODEL.md` |
| API / worker messages | Worker method names, payloads, or Comlink contract changed? | `packages/core` exports, nested `AGENTS.md`, `docs/VAULT_FORMAT.md` if persisted |
| Folder structure | New routes, features, packages, or moved modules? | `docs/getting-started.md`, `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md` |
| Environment variables | New env vars or config (even if optional)? | `README.md`, `docs/getting-started.md`, `.env.example` if added |
| Testing instructions | New test commands, packages, or required setup? | `CONTRIBUTING.md`, package `AGENTS.md` |
| Known limitations | New caveats, unsupported flows, or partial features? | `README.md` or scoped note in final report |
| Migration notes | Breaking vault, API, or persisted format change? | `docs/VAULT_FORMAT.md` + migration section |

If nothing in a row changed, **skip that doc**. Mention "no doc update required" in the final report.

## Do not

- Rewrite entire docs when a section update suffices
- Mark ROADMAP items complete without explicit permission
- Bump vault envelope `version` for additive payload fields with safe defaults
- Weaken root security in AGENTS or `.mdc` text
- Leave critical policy only in `.cursor/rules` — reinforce root/nested `AGENTS.md`
- Add documentation-only commits for trivial code edits (typos, formatting)

## Pattern anchors

### BAD

```markdown
<!-- Unprompted full rewrite after a one-line UI copy change -->
Rewrote docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/SECURITY.md, and ROADMAP.md
```

### GOOD

```markdown
<!-- Scoped update after worker contract change -->
Updated docs/ARCHITECTURE.md § Crypto Boundary — added exportRecoveryPhrase to worker API list.
No changes to README or ROADMAP.
```
